      "text": "Let $\\angle A = \\beta$, $\\angle B = \\alpha$ and $\\angle C = 90^\\circ$. \n[asy]\nsize(250);\npair A, B, C, D, X;\nA=(0,0);\nB=(0,12);\nC=(-16,0);\nD=(-35,0);\nX=(-16-16*cos(beta),-16*sin(beta));\ndraw(A--B--D--A);\ndraw(B--C);\ndraw(A--X,N);\ndraw(X--B, red);\ndraw(X--D,red);\ndraw((0,1.5)--(-1.5,1.5)--(-1.5,0));\nlabel(\"$37$\", (B+D)/2, NW);\nlabel(\"$19$\", (C+D)/2, S);\nlabel(\"$16$\", (A+C)/2, S);\nlabel(\"$\\alpha$\", (0,2), NE);\nlabel(\"$\\beta$\", (2,0), SE);\nlabel(\"$\\alpha$\", (2,0), SE);\nlabel(\"A\", A, SE);\nlabel(\"B\", B, NE);\nlabel(\"D\", D, SW);\nlabel(\"C\", C, S);\nlabel(\"$x$\", (D-X)/2, S);\nlabel(\"$y$\", (X-D)/2, NW);\n[/asy] Now, $\\triangle ABC$ has sides $19$ and $x - 16$; the hypotenuse $37$.\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{By the Pythagorean Theorem,} \\\\\n37^2 &= x^2 - 32x + 256 \\\\\n1369 &= x^2 - 32x + 256 \\\\\nx^2 - 32x - 1113 &= 0\n\\end{align*}\nBy the quadratic formula, \\[x = \\frac{32 \\pm \\sqrt{(-32)^2 - 4(1)(-1113)}}{2(1)} = \\frac{32 \\pm \\sqrt{1369}}{2} = \\frac{32 \\pm 37}{2}.\\] We take $x = 34$ since $x$ represents a length.\n\nSimilarly $\\triangle ABD$ has sides $16$ and $y - 19$; the hypotenuse $37.$\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{By the Pythagorean Theorem,} \\\\\n37^2 &= y^2 - 32y + 361 \\\\\n1369 &= y^2 - 32y + 361 \\\\\ny^2 - 32y - 908 &= 0\n  \\end{align*}\nBy the quadratic formula, \\[y = \\frac{32 \\pm \\sqrt{(-32)^2 - 4(1)(-908)}}{2(1)} = \\frac{32 \\pm \\sqrt{1369}}{2} = \\frac{32 \\pm 37}{2}.\\] We take $y = 25$ since $y$ represents a length.\n[asy]\nsize(170);\npair A, B, C, D, X;\nA=(0,0);\nB=(0,12);\nC=(-16,0);\nD=(-35,0);\nX=(-16-16*cos(beta),-16*sin(beta));\ndraw(A--B--D--A);\ndraw(B--C);\ndraw(A--X,N);\ndraw(X--B, red);\ndraw(X--D,red);\ndraw((0,1.5)--(-1.5,1.5)--(-1.5,0));\nlabel(\"$37$\", (B+D)/2, NW);\nlabel(\"$19$\", (C+D)/2, S);\nlabel(\"$16$\", (A+C)/2, S);\nlabel(\"$\\alpha$\", (0,2), NE);\nlabel(\"$\\beta$\", (2,0), SE);\nlabel(\"$\\alpha$\", (2,0), SE);\nlabel(\"$\\beta$\", (2,0), SE);\nlabel(\"$x$\", (D-X)/2, S);\nlabel(\"$y$\", (X-D)/2, NW);\nlabel(\"$A$\", A, SW);\nlabel(\"$B$\", B, NE);\nlabel(\"$D$\", D, SW);\nlabel(\"$C$\", C, S);\nlabel(\"$x - 16$\",(0,19),W);\nlabel(\"$y - 19$\",(-16,y-19), N);\n[/asy]\n\nHence, \\[BC = \\sqrt{x^2 - y^2} = \\sqrt{34^2 - 25^2} = \\boxed{57}. \\]. The answer is 57",
